# Verification & completion report

No substantial task is complete because code was written. Verify the actual result.

## Verification levels (do not confuse)

1. Source inspection · 2. Static analysis · 3. Unit · 4. Types · 5. Integration · 6. Contract · 7. Build · 8. Actual UI · 9. Hosted env · 10. Physical hardware

Examples: TS build ≠ tenant isolation; unit pass ≠ live email; frontend build ≠ correct Convex deploy; staging ≠ production readiness.

## After changes

- Run relevant tests (`pnpm test`, targeted vitest). Do not weaken/skip tests to pass.
- For UI: open the route, check console, verify mobile when claimed.
- State NOT VERIFIED where evidence is missing. Never invent counts, URLs, or logs.

## Substantial tasks require this exact report

Feature/bug/refactor/schema/auth/API/deploy/config/test-suite/docs-status work. Skip only for trivial Q&A.

### 1. TASK SUMMARY
- Task / Objective / Final status: COMPLETE | PARTIALLY COMPLETE | BLOCKED / Outcome

### 2. FILES CHANGED
List created/modified/deleted with brief why (or state none).

### 3. IMPLEMENTATION DETAILS
What, how, components affected, design decisions, compatibility.

### 4. VERIFICATION AND TEST RESULTS
Table: Check | Command | Result PASS/FAIL/NOT RUN | Evidence

### 5. ACTUAL BEHAVIOR VERIFICATION
Routes/interactions/console/backend env/real data — or NOT VERIFIED.

### 6. SECURITY AND DATA-INTEGRITY CHECK
Authz, tenant isolation, persistence, secrets, credentials, deploy impact; any destructive ops.

### 7. DEPLOYMENT AND ENVIRONMENT STATUS
Modified or not; build target; URL; Convex id; commit; rollback — or NOT DEPLOYED.

### 8. KNOWN ISSUES AND LIMITATIONS
Unresolved, deferred, missing evidence, exceptions.

### 9. DOCUMENTATION UPDATED
Files touched / none.

### 10. FINAL ENGINEERING VERDICT
COMPLETE — VERIFIED | COMPLETE WITH DOCUMENTED LIMITATIONS | PARTIALLY COMPLETE | BLOCKED | FAILED

### 11. NEXT ACTIONS
Safe now · needs owner approval · needs production auth · needs hardware auth
